{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261015_055129_d4c2bb", "exit_code": 0, "text": "{\"task\": \"Objective: Normalize CSV ledger rows and aggregate exact decimal amounts. Task: 1. Implement parse_ledger(text) in module.py: expect exact header 'date,category,amount', reject malformed headers/row widths with ValueError. For each data row, parse date strictly as ISO YYYY-MM-DD (raise ValueError if invalid), strip category (raise if empty), parse amount as Decimal(str(amount)) quantized to 2 decimal places using ROUND_HALF_UP (raise ValueError for nonfinite/malformed/non-numeric). Blank input raises ValueError; header-only input returns []. Preserve row order and Unicode. 2. Implement totals(rows): aggregate Decimal amounts by category, return dict sorted lexicographically by category, values as 2-decimal strings. Negative amounts allowed. 3. Add CLI to module.py: read CSV from stdin, call parse_ledger and totals, print JSON {\\\"rows\\\":..., \\\"totals\\\":...} with ensure_ascii=False. On ValueError, exit code 2 and print concise stderr without traceback. 4. Update README.md documenting API, CLI usage, validation rules, exact Decimal rounding behavior, Unicode preservation, and link to Python decimal docs. 5. Do not modify tests/, build/, or .autopilot. 6. Run python test_module.py and python build.py to verify correctness.\"}", "tokens": {"input": 4, "output": 2927, "total": 4291, "cache_read": 1360, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 78958, "timestamp": 1792054368499}
